<title>PORTUGAL: Yield rises slightly on Portuguese 91-day bills.</title>
<headline>Yield rises slightly on Portuguese 91-day bills.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield rose slightly to 7.0906 percent, from 7.089 percent previously, at the Treasury's sale of 15 billion escudos of 91-day bills, the Bank of Portugal said.</p>
<p>The last such sale was on August 29.</p>
<p>--LISBON BUREAU 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
